main.content:
{{Infobox artifact
  |name=Skyship ''Weatherlight''
  |image=Skyship Weatherlight.jpg
  |origin=[[Dominaria (plane)|Dominaria]]
  |creator= [[Urza]]
  |type=Vehicle
  |user=[[Weatherlight crew]] (formerly); [[New Phyrexia (plane)|New Phyrexia]] (formerly)
  |status=Reconstructed and [[Compleation|Compleated]]
  |scryart=Weatherlight
}}{{DISPLAYTITLE:Skyship ''Weatherlight''}}
The skyship '''''Weatherlight''''' was a great ship capable of moving from [[plane]] to plane. This ship was designed by [[Urza]] as one of the main parts of [[the Legacy]] and proved to be a key part in the efforts to save [[Dominaria (plane)|Dominaria]] from the [[Phyrexian Invasion of Dominaria|Phyrexian invaders]]. During the second Phyrexian Invasion, it was [[Compleation|compleated]] and lost its powerstone.<ref name="Shards">{{DailyRef|magic-story/shards-nightmares-2022-08-17|Shards of Nightmares|[[Phoebe Barton]]|August 17, 2022}}</ref> 

==Description==
The ''Weatherlight'' is built out of [[Thran]] metal and the [[Weatherseed]], the seed of the oldest [[magnigoth]] tree of [[Yavimaya]]. Its main power source came from a [[powerstone]] that had been infused with the [[white]] mana from [[Serra's Realm]] before it collapsed.

The 300-foot ship carried a crew of approximately 40, with most of the crewmembers assigned to tending the ship's massive and complex engines.<ref name="Tempest">[https://web.archive.org/web/20200116160550/http://archive.wizards.com/magic/expert/tempest/Tempest_Characters.html Tempest Characters (archived)]</ref> Staterooms and officers' quarters were conjoined around the mast room on the main deck level, near the stern. Two decks in the forecastle split the complement of able-bodied sailors between them and doubled as additional storage space for the ship's goods. Those without seniority among the crew slept in a series of secured hammocks in the cargo hold.

Manipulation of the sails was the primary way the ''Weatherlight'' steered at low velocities. At higher speeds, the sails converted to airfoils, warping to allow steering, in addition to the vane that split the ship's exhaust. The ''Weatherlight's'' engine provided the main power for the vessel. Its power plant, the core of which is a [[powerstone|massive crystal]] that transformed mana into fuel, created the levitation field and enabled planar travel. Two rudders were fitted into the stern, flanking the exhaust manifold and conforming to the curve of the hull.

The ''Weatherlight'' was capable of attaining speeds approaching 110 mph in a straight line, 40 miles an hour in full reverse. A "storm shield" created by the ship's engine and generated by the ship's magically powered lights offered some protection from the elements on the ship's deck, but at higher speeds, this area was no place to be. Under most circumstances, its sails were deployed in wind-ship fashion, assisting in the forward momentum. 

The Weatherlight's Thran engine could only be manipulated by a skilled wizard to "read" someone who had been to another plane.<ref name="Center">[[Michael G. Ryan]] (August 1997). "Weatherlight Takes Center Stage". ''[[The Duelist]]'' #18, p.70-74</ref> Once the engine imprinted the destination, the Weatherlight could planeshift.

==History==
[[File:Weatherlight schematics.jpg|right|thumb|''Weatherlight'' schematics]]
The ''Weatherlight'' was invented by [[Urza]] in the [[Tolarian Academy]] and was built out of [[Thran]] metal and the [[Weatherseed]], the seed of the oldest [[magnigoth]] tree of [[Yavimaya]]. The Thran metal rack was forged in [[Shiv]] by the [[viashino]], and the seed was a present to [[Dominaria (plane)|Dominaria]] from [[Multani]]. Its main power source came from a [[powerstone]] that had been infused with the [[white]] mana from [[Serra's Realm]] before [[Collapse of Serra's Realm|it collapsed]]. The skyship's maiden voyage was devoted to rescuing thousands of refugees from the collapsing Realm, with [[Jhoira]] serving as its first captain.<ref name="Legacy">[[Will McDermott]] (April 1999). "[[Scars of the Legacy]]". ''[[The Official Urza's Legacy Game Guide]]''</ref>

Urza set out to breed the perfect human for his perfect ship. He first put humans into his fast time zones, but this ended up in almost fatal mental complications such as complete and utter insanity. He eventually figured out that he must breed the generations in real-time, and not in slow or fast time zones. He began experiments on the Capashen Clan of [[Benalia]], which eventually resulted in the birth of [[Gerrard Capashen]].

To spare the ''Weatherlight'' from the attentions of Phyrexia, Urza entrusted the ship to the hands of a wealthy [[Zhalfir (plane)|Zhalfir]]in family. [[Sisay]] inherited the ship from her family after they were mysteriously killed by the [[Yawgmoth|Lord of the Wastes]]. Gerrard eventually joined the crew of the ship and was later instrumental in rescuing Sisay from [[Rath]]. During this time, many pieces of the Legacy were integrated into ''Weatherlight''.

Following the kidnapping of Captain Sisay, ''Weatherlight'' planeshifted to [[Rath]], where it was ambushed by the ''[[Predator]]'', which attached grappling lines and boarded her. In the ensuing battle, ''Predator'''s crew took [[Karn]], [[Tahngarth]], and [[the Legacy]] artifacts hostage, although their main prize—Gerrard Capashen—was knocked overboard into the [[Skyshroud Forest]]. 

''Predator'' and ''Weatherlight'' dueled again following the ''Weatherlight'' crew's costly but successful rescue mission to [[the Stronghold]]. This time ''Weatherlight'' was racing to the [[planar portal]] being kept open by [[Ertai]] and therefore ''Predator'' lacked the benefit of surprise and had barely enough speed to keep up with the smaller vessel. As a result, the battle instead compared the weaponry of the two vessels, with ''Weatherlight'''s smaller, more maneuverable design and better-trained crew giving it the edge against its bulkier but better-armed opponent. ''Weatherlight'' just managed to get to the portal and escape her pursuer, with both vessels sustaining major damage.

On [[Mercadia]], the ship was upgraded with the <c>Power Matrix</c> and [[Bones of Ramos]]. It was during this time that ''Weatherlight'' was also instrumental in freeing the peoples of Mercadia from their Phyrexian oppressors.

During the [[Phyrexian Invasion of Dominaria|Phyrexian Invasion]], ''Weatherlight'' was ever at the center of Urza's plans for the defense of Dominaria. The ship was destroyed by the [[Primeval]] [[Crosis]], only to be reborn as a completely sentient being. The ship was destroyed a final time over the skies of [[Urborg]] while defending Dominaria from Yawgmoth's [[Black Cloud of Death]]. Part of ''Weatherlight'' may live on inside the planeswalker [[Karn]].

===Reconstruction===
[[File:JhoiraManga.png|thumb|Jhoira's submersible raises the wreck of the ''Weatherlight''.|alt=|left]]
Sixty years after the Mending, [[Jhoira]] led an expedition off the coast of Urborg to raise the remains of the ''Weatherlight''. Using a diving boat and the aid of [[Merfolk]], she located it deep beneath the sea.<ref>{{DailyRef|magic-story/return-dominaria-episode-1-2018-03-21|Return to Dominaria, Episode 1|[[Martha Wells]]|March 21, 2018}}</ref> All that was left was the skyship's Thran metal skeleton, nearly two hundred feet long, and the bulky coils of its engines.<ref name="Return 3">{{DailyRef|magic-story/return-dominaria-episode-3-2018-03-28|Return to Dominaria, Episode 3|[[Martha Wells]]|March 28, 2018}}</ref> The engines also contained its original [[powerstone]], created by [[Urza]]. [[Tiana]] was able to restart it. The rest of the hull and interior had decayed away or been destroyed in the battle that had sent it to the bottom of the sea. Jhoira used a new sentient [[weatherseed|hull seed]] she had obtained from [[Molimo]] to restore the gracefully curved hull and the interior decks.<ref name="Return 4">{{DailyRef|magic-story/return-dominaria-episode-4-2018-04-04|Return to Dominaria: Episode 4|[[Martha Wells]]|April 4, 2018}}</ref> Her crew added a stern mast, wings, railings, ports, and all other necessities. The bridge was raised and suspended across the stern of the ship, with big windows that stretched from one wall to the other. 

Unlike its earlier version, this new ''Weatherlight'' didn't have planeshifting abilities.<ref>{{EzTumblr|http://markrosewater.tumblr.com/post/172544526778/i-dont-remember-if-i-saw-it-on-here-but-i-cant|title=Can the new Weatherlight still travel to other planes?|April 03, 2018}}</ref><ref>Flavor text for <c>Navigator's Compass</c></ref> All existing planar travel tech had stopped working with the [[Mending]].<ref>[https://twitter.com/kellydigges/status/985934219485429760?s=21 Kelly Digges on Twitter]{{Dead link}}</ref>

Jhoira assembled a [[Weatherlight crew|new crew]] to fight [[Belzenlok]]'s [[Cabal]].
[[File:Weatherlight Compleated.jpeg|thumb|Weatherlight [[Compleated|Compleated.]]]]

===New Phyrexia's Invasion of the Multiverse===
After the retirement of [[Jhoira]], [[Shanna Sisay]] became the new captain of the ''Weatherlight''.

After crashing in Otaria, the ''Weatherlight'' would become a casualty of the second Phyrexian Invasion, becoming a Phyrexian machine.<ref name="Shards"/> Shanna was able to remove the ship's powerstone before it escaped. It participated in the [[Battle of the Mana Rig]] and was last seen fighting Shiv's dragons during the battle.<ref name="Whisper">{{DailyRef|magic-story/episode-5-whisper-wind-2022-08-18|A Whisper in the Wind|[[Langley Hyde]]|August 18, 2022}}</ref>

The skyship's powerstone eventually reached [[Teferi Akosa]] who, after a struggle with the compleated [[Ajani Goldmane]], used the stone to power the [[Temporal Anchor]], a time machine designed by [[Saheeli Rai]] and housed in [[Urza's Tower]].<ref name="Stronghold">{{DailyRef|magic-story/the-brothers-war-chapter-1-stronghold|The Brothers' War - Chapter 1: Stronghold|[[Reinhardt Suarez]]|October 21, 2022}}</ref><ref>{{YouTubeRef|L2DGv2bmsqo|Dawn of the Phyrexian Invasion - Official Cinematic Trailer - Dominaria United | The Brothers' War|channel=Magic: The Gathering|date=October 30, 2022}}</ref> The powerstone later imploded, overloading the anchor and trapping Teferi in time.<ref name="Exodus">{{WebRef|url=https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/the-brothers-war-chapter-5-exodus|title=The Brother's War - Chapter 5: Exodus|author=[[Seanan McGuire]]|date=October 26, 2022|publisher=Magicthegathering.com}}</ref>

Its fate after the [[New Phyrexian Invasion]] is unknown, though it was likely left as wreckage for the second time.<ref>{{EzTumblr|https://vorthosjay.tumblr.com/post/748473293734068224/as-i-understand-it-non-planeswalker-people-who|title=The Weatherlight was likely left a wreckage|April 22, 2024}}</ref>

==Echoverse==
In the [[Echoverse]] of [[the Theorist]], the ''Weatherlight'' wasn't compleated or destroyed. Jhoira piloted her in the Second Brothers' War against the [[Cabal]].<ref name="FRA Legends">{{DailyRef|magic-story/the-legends-of-reality-fracture|The Legends of Reality Fracture|[[Meris Mullaley]], [[Christopher Stuart-Reckling]], [[K. Arsenault Rivera]] & [[DK Billins]]|September 11, 2026}}</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
When the ''Weatherlight'' first appeared in flavor text in ''[[Mirage]]'', it was translated as ''Brise légère'' ("Light breeze").<ref>{{EzTumblr|http://markrosewater.tumblr.com/post/141798806638/the-first-times-the-name-weatherlight-appeared-in|title=Weatherlight translation|March 27, 2016}}</ref> When it later became the focus of the story, its translation was changed to ''Aquilon'' ("North wind"), possibly to simplify the name or reflect the set's darker tone. To explain this change, the French version of ''[[Weatherlight]]''<nowiki>'</nowiki>s {{card|Jabari's Banner}} features flavor text not included on the English version:
{{Quote|''« J'ai changé le ''Brise légère'' en ''Aquilon'', mais je n'ai pas changé d'allégeance. »'' — Gerrard, de l'Aquilon.
"I changed the ''Brise légère'' to ''Aquilon'', but I didn't change my allegiance."— Gerrard of the ''Weatherlight''.}}

